1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:17,180
Me and Kobayashi got into a fight.

2
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:19,880
Kobayashi, you're a dummy!

3
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:21,480
You butt-face!

4
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,640
I'm still scared to go back home,

5
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,440
but the sky is so dark and I'm getting sleepy.

6
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:31,100
I'm going to go find somewhere brighter.

7
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:52,440
So many humans, lots of big beltings.

8
00:02:26,967 --> 00:02:29,847
What is this loud voice?

9
00:02:34,427 --> 00:02:36,327
It looks fun.

10
00:02:44,667 --> 00:02:46,667
My tummy's hungry.

11
00:02:48,147 --> 00:02:49,707
Thanks for coming by.

12
00:02:49,887 --> 00:02:50,867
That looks good.

13
00:02:51,107 --> 00:02:51,827
Appreciate it.

14
00:02:51,827 --> 00:02:53,427
595 yen.

15
00:02:54,827 --> 00:02:56,727
Hey there, what do you want?

16
00:02:57,567 --> 00:02:59,067
Oh, Japanese money.

17
00:02:59,567 --> 00:03:01,667
Sorry, but I'm afraid you can't use that here.

18
00:03:01,987 --> 00:03:03,747
I'm afraid we don't accept the end.

19
00:03:04,627 --> 00:03:05,767
He talks funny.

20
00:03:06,147 --> 00:03:06,987
Are you alone here?

21
00:03:07,567 --> 00:03:08,447
Where's your mom?

22
00:03:08,547 --> 00:03:09,687
Why are you always acting like that?

23
00:03:09,707 --> 00:03:11,707
Let's go get some U.S. dollars from your mom.

24
00:03:11,727 --> 00:03:12,287
I'm always serious.

25
00:03:12,287 --> 00:03:14,687
The hot dogs won't go anywhere, so take your time.

26
00:03:15,267 --> 00:03:17,367
I'll give you a good discount when you come back.

27
00:03:17,547 --> 00:03:18,387
Let me tell you.

28
00:03:20,487 --> 00:03:21,847
No, I totally get it.

29
00:03:22,047 --> 00:03:22,727
What's the matter?

30
00:03:23,407 --> 00:03:23,827
You okay?

31
00:03:24,167 --> 00:03:25,687
Did you space out or something?

32
00:03:25,987 --> 00:03:26,327
Yes.

33
00:03:26,327 --> 00:03:29,567
Still yen.

34
00:03:29,847 --> 00:03:32,547
You need to pay with our country's money if you want to buy stuff.

35
00:03:37,927 --> 00:03:39,727
I can't use money here.

36
00:03:39,727 --> 00:03:42,967
Not many humans on this street.

37
00:03:45,187 --> 00:03:46,127
Somebody help me, please!

38
00:03:46,127 --> 00:03:47,527
Get back here, you little brat!

39
00:03:51,527 --> 00:03:53,047
Stop running right now!

40
00:03:53,127 --> 00:03:53,447
No!

41
00:03:53,927 --> 00:03:55,387
You'll never catch me!

42
00:03:55,907 --> 00:03:56,827
What you doing?

43
00:03:56,827 --> 00:04:01,227
I'm sorry I didn't see you there!

44
00:04:01,447 --> 00:04:02,347
Why are you running?

45
00:04:02,687 --> 00:04:03,427
Isn't it obvious?

46
00:04:04,067 --> 00:04:05,007
They're being chased!

47
00:04:05,247 --> 00:04:06,247
Those guys are bad!

48
00:04:06,527 --> 00:04:07,387
I gotta go!

49
00:04:07,507 --> 00:04:08,147
I get that.

50
00:04:08,147 --> 00:04:09,707
I'll save you.

51
00:04:09,707 --> 00:04:11,327
You'll save me!

52
00:04:11,387 --> 00:04:11,887
But help!

53
00:04:11,887 --> 00:04:12,907
Out of the way, kid!

54
00:04:13,047 --> 00:04:13,607
Move!

55
00:04:17,607 --> 00:04:19,747
What the heck?

56
00:04:19,747 --> 00:04:20,127
Michael!

57
00:04:20,567 --> 00:04:22,007
Who is that brat?

58
00:04:22,007 --> 00:04:23,867
What the hell did she just do?

59
00:04:24,187 --> 00:04:25,967
How dare you hurt Michael like that!

60
00:04:26,067 --> 00:04:27,307
He's not feeling well!

61
00:04:27,667 --> 00:04:29,167
He already had the runs today!

62
00:04:29,287 --> 00:04:29,467
Oh!

63
00:04:29,967 --> 00:04:30,827
Hey, wait!

64
00:04:31,367 --> 00:04:32,127
Let's go.

65
00:04:32,127 --> 00:04:41,607
You saved my life!

66
00:04:42,027 --> 00:04:42,647
Thank you!

67
00:04:46,087 --> 00:04:48,847
You're freakishly strong for someone your age, know that?

68
00:04:49,607 --> 00:04:50,287
Wait a sec!

69
00:04:50,507 --> 00:04:51,667
Are we in New York?

70
00:04:53,667 --> 00:04:54,147
Hi!

71
00:04:54,307 --> 00:04:54,967
My name's Chloe!

72
00:04:55,847 --> 00:04:56,327
Kana.

73
00:04:57,047 --> 00:04:57,507
Kana!

74
00:04:58,767 --> 00:05:00,907
Chloe, why were they chasing you?

75
00:05:00,907 --> 00:05:02,107
They kidnapped me!

76
00:05:02,287 --> 00:05:04,187
And I just found out that they're in the Mafia.

77
00:05:04,747 --> 00:05:06,067
So I'm trying to stay low-key.

78
00:05:06,527 --> 00:05:07,007
Mafia?

79
00:05:07,227 --> 00:05:08,007
Is it bad?

80
00:05:08,287 --> 00:05:08,587
Yeah!

81
00:05:08,847 --> 00:05:11,367
That's why I took off running when I thought the coast was clear!

82
00:05:11,747 --> 00:05:12,447
Poor Chloe.

83
00:05:13,147 --> 00:05:15,507
My dad is the CEO of an important company.

84
00:05:16,007 --> 00:05:17,647
He publicly opposes the Mafia.

85
00:05:18,707 --> 00:05:20,307
They're using me to get to him!

86
00:05:20,467 --> 00:05:21,387
They're not here now!

87
00:05:21,467 --> 00:05:22,087
Let's go play!

88
00:05:22,247 --> 00:05:22,467
Huh?

89
00:05:22,587 --> 00:05:23,727
You wanna go where?

90
00:05:23,987 --> 00:05:24,207
What?

91
00:05:24,667 --> 00:05:25,447
I'm bored.

92
00:05:26,007 --> 00:05:26,887
Let's go play.

93
00:05:26,887 --> 00:05:27,387
Huh?

94
00:05:31,127 --> 00:05:32,027
Yeah, okay.

95
00:05:32,847 --> 00:05:34,347
I can play with you.

96
00:05:34,807 --> 00:05:35,367
Huh?

97
00:05:36,727 --> 00:05:37,647
You're hungry.

98
00:05:37,807 --> 00:05:39,167
I'll buy you some lunch as a thanks.

99
00:05:40,607 --> 00:05:41,127
Yay!

100
00:05:42,487 --> 00:05:43,567
Let's go, Chloe.

101
00:05:44,447 --> 00:05:44,707
Huh?

102
00:05:44,827 --> 00:05:45,267
Okay.

103
00:05:45,967 --> 00:05:47,527
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.

104
00:05:48,067 --> 00:05:49,347
This is perfect.

105
00:05:49,707 --> 00:05:50,927
It can stay out longer.

106
00:05:51,187 --> 00:05:52,807
Anything to keep from going home.

107
00:05:52,807 --> 00:05:57,507
A black card?

108
00:05:57,507 --> 00:06:01,687
I'm sorry, we don't take credit cards at the hot dog stand.

109
00:06:05,687 --> 00:06:08,467
I usually don't carry much cash on me.

110
00:06:10,547 --> 00:06:13,387
Anyway, this is my first time exploring New York City.

111
00:06:13,387 --> 00:06:16,627
I usually just stay on our mansion grounds and don't go anywhere.

112
00:06:17,147 --> 00:06:18,647
Does this mean you're rich, Chloe?

113
00:06:18,967 --> 00:06:20,067
Uh, yeah, I guess.

114
00:06:20,287 --> 00:06:21,487
So you scream a lot?

115
00:06:21,947 --> 00:06:22,547
Like her?

116
00:06:22,547 --> 00:06:23,747
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

117
00:06:23,747 --> 00:06:24,307
What...

118
00:06:24,307 --> 00:06:25,447
What's this happen?

119
00:06:25,447 --> 00:06:27,667
Boy, she doesn't sound very happy.

120
00:06:28,607 --> 00:06:30,507
She plays with me a lot, too.

121
00:06:30,807 --> 00:06:32,367
There are all kinds of people, huh?

122
00:06:32,367 --> 00:06:33,367
Yeah.

123
00:06:33,367 --> 00:06:49,327
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

124
00:06:49,327 --> 00:07:19,307
Let's get started.

125
00:07:19,327 --> 00:07:49,307
Let's get started.

126
00:07:49,327 --> 00:07:50,387
I'm sorry.

127
00:07:50,867 --> 00:07:54,047
I had a fight with Kobayashi and ran away from home.

128
00:07:54,547 --> 00:07:56,787
But it was all because of something I did.

129
00:07:57,547 --> 00:07:58,547
It's my fault.

130
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:00,527
I should head back now.

131
00:08:00,527 --> 00:08:08,487
Are you sure?

132
00:08:09,387 --> 00:08:10,967
Are you sure it's safe?

133
00:08:12,587 --> 00:08:13,387
What if?

134
00:08:13,707 --> 00:08:15,667
What if they're still mad when you get back?

135
00:08:15,907 --> 00:08:18,227
What if they won't forgive you after you apologize?

136
00:08:18,707 --> 00:08:20,027
Doesn't that scare you?

137
00:08:20,027 --> 00:08:24,207
Yes, it does.

138
00:08:25,107 --> 00:08:29,247
But I'm more scared of not having a home and nowhere to go.

139
00:08:33,167 --> 00:08:33,887
Chloe?

140
00:08:35,807 --> 00:08:36,807
Come on.

141
00:08:37,667 --> 00:08:38,647
Let's go home.

142
00:08:38,647 --> 00:08:42,987
Listen.

143
00:08:44,987 --> 00:08:47,367
Kana, I...

144
00:08:47,367 --> 00:08:48,647
I can't just...

145
00:08:48,647 --> 00:08:55,587
Chloe!

146
00:08:55,587 --> 00:09:19,387
Geez, I never knew kidnapping a crafty runaway would be such a boring and easy job.

147
00:09:20,927 --> 00:09:23,487
I think a little punishment should liven things up.

148
00:09:23,487 --> 00:09:25,787
Shut it and give me the tape.

149
00:09:26,127 --> 00:09:27,167
Right here, Michael.

150
00:09:28,107 --> 00:09:31,027
Hey, just make sure you don't damage the goods.

151
00:09:32,527 --> 00:09:35,187
One tiny arm ain't gonna make much of a difference.

152
00:09:36,227 --> 00:09:38,787
I was wrong. I never should have run away.

153
00:09:39,067 --> 00:09:41,207
I would do anything to be back home.

154
00:09:41,447 --> 00:09:42,927
I'm so sorry, Papa!

155
00:09:45,247 --> 00:09:46,567
What the? What?

156
00:09:46,567 --> 00:09:47,607
It's so dark.

157
00:09:47,947 --> 00:09:49,487
Go check the breaker, you dope.

158
00:09:49,607 --> 00:09:49,947
Breaker?

159
00:09:50,167 --> 00:09:51,667
I'll go do it. Stay here.

160
00:09:51,667 --> 00:09:53,027
Ow! That hurts.

161
00:09:53,027 --> 00:09:54,167
Lock your step!

162
00:09:56,007 --> 00:09:57,427
Sorry about that.

163
00:09:57,427 --> 00:10:27,407
Oh, my God.

164
00:10:27,427 --> 00:10:28,987
Don't eat me! I taste gross!

165
00:10:29,667 --> 00:10:30,267
Chloe.

166
00:10:30,907 --> 00:10:33,347
Huh? I know that voice.

167
00:10:34,687 --> 00:10:35,907
Let's go home.

168
00:10:36,307 --> 00:10:36,607
Wait.

169
00:10:37,467 --> 00:10:37,887
Kana?

170
00:10:42,147 --> 00:10:46,787
Amazing!

171
00:10:47,267 --> 00:10:48,467
Am I dreaming right now?

172
00:10:49,327 --> 00:10:51,627
Or maybe those jerks actually killed me?

173
00:10:51,887 --> 00:10:53,547
Are we flying around heaven, Kana?

174
00:10:54,427 --> 00:10:55,847
It's not a dream.

175
00:10:55,847 --> 00:10:57,867
Can you tell me where you live?

176
00:10:58,047 --> 00:11:00,227
I'm in Minnesota, so probably there.

177
00:11:00,707 --> 00:11:02,287
It's just past those big lakes.

178
00:11:03,227 --> 00:11:03,947
I see them.

179
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:08,027
You're so soft and so warm.

180
00:11:08,027 --> 00:11:11,187
I lied to you.

181
00:11:11,727 --> 00:11:12,587
I ran away.

182
00:11:13,207 --> 00:11:14,747
They didn't kidnap me.

183
00:11:16,087 --> 00:11:17,047
You too?

184
00:11:17,767 --> 00:11:18,407
Yeah.

185
00:11:18,947 --> 00:11:20,367
I had a fight with my papa.

186
00:11:20,987 --> 00:11:22,087
I need to apologize.

187
00:11:22,927 --> 00:11:24,127
But I don't know what to say.

188
00:11:25,707 --> 00:11:26,707
Me neither.

189
00:11:26,707 --> 00:11:33,267
But if someone's still there after things get bad.

190
00:11:35,167 --> 00:11:37,187
Even when you get mad at them.

191
00:11:40,147 --> 00:11:42,687
And say mean things like you hate them.

192
00:11:42,687 --> 00:11:49,827
If there's somebody who stays, I'm sure it'll be okay.

193
00:11:50,967 --> 00:11:51,407
Yeah.

194
00:11:53,507 --> 00:11:55,687
Are you ready to go home too, Kana?

195
00:11:56,707 --> 00:11:57,227
Yeah.

196
00:11:57,767 --> 00:11:58,907
Will I see you again?

197
00:11:59,347 --> 00:12:01,627
If you want, I'll give you my address.

198
00:12:02,627 --> 00:12:03,807
You have an address?

199
00:12:03,807 --> 00:12:20,227
Oh, hi.

200
00:12:20,447 --> 00:12:22,207
And where have you been all this time?

201
00:12:22,587 --> 00:12:23,507
Lady Toru.

202
00:12:24,207 --> 00:12:25,507
I'm so sorry.

203
00:12:25,507 --> 00:12:29,327
Well, I'm not the one you should be apologizing to.

204
00:12:30,807 --> 00:12:32,127
I know you're right.

205
00:12:32,527 --> 00:12:33,447
Where's Kobayashi?

206
00:12:46,247 --> 00:12:48,767
Have you decided what you're going to say when she wakes up?

207
00:12:49,787 --> 00:12:50,787
No idea.

208
00:12:50,987 --> 00:12:52,727
Unless Kobayashi said the same thing.

209
00:12:55,507 --> 00:13:10,767
I was watching you the whole time.

210
00:13:10,767 --> 00:13:11,187
Oh.

211
00:13:18,407 --> 00:13:20,027
Okay, I'm heading out.

212
00:13:21,387 --> 00:13:22,707
Be safe out there.

213
00:13:22,707 --> 00:13:25,927
See you later, Miss Kobayashi.

214
00:13:26,207 --> 00:13:27,547
I'm off to work now.

215
00:13:28,207 --> 00:13:29,147
Okay, take care.

216
00:13:32,947 --> 00:13:34,227
It's so hot.

217
00:13:35,767 --> 00:13:37,207
Oh, hey, Kana.

218
00:13:37,347 --> 00:13:37,927
You're awake.

219
00:13:38,207 --> 00:13:38,907
Good morning.

220
00:13:39,567 --> 00:13:39,987
Morning.

221
00:13:41,447 --> 00:13:43,287
Kobayashi, are you off work today?

222
00:13:43,547 --> 00:13:44,647
Yes, good night.

223
00:13:46,267 --> 00:13:46,707
Oh.

224
00:13:47,427 --> 00:13:49,287
I was super busy until yesterday.

225
00:13:50,227 --> 00:13:51,347
Death March style?

226
00:13:51,347 --> 00:13:52,667
Super Death March style.

227
00:14:03,847 --> 00:14:05,607
Next up, we have Kobayashi.

228
00:14:05,847 --> 00:14:06,447
Kobayashi.

229
00:14:06,447 --> 00:14:07,907
Hello, friends.

230
00:14:08,007 --> 00:14:08,827
Kobayashi here.

231
00:14:09,087 --> 00:14:09,727
Today we're trying to...

232
00:14:09,727 --> 00:14:11,467
Where are Lady Toru and Yolobu?

233
00:14:11,847 --> 00:14:14,467
They're both working until this evening for a change.

234
00:14:14,467 --> 00:14:22,687
Are you just going to laze around the house all day long?

235
00:14:22,987 --> 00:14:23,427
Mm-hmm.

236
00:14:24,147 --> 00:14:25,807
I'm going to be super lazy.

237
00:14:26,467 --> 00:14:28,647
Might be a good day for you to go play with Saekoa.

238
00:14:28,647 --> 00:14:30,367
I can't.

239
00:14:30,747 --> 00:14:33,707
Saekoa said she's going on a family vacation today.

240
00:14:34,287 --> 00:14:36,447
Looks like a boring day for you, then.

241
00:14:39,107 --> 00:14:40,327
Bean jam, huh?

242
00:14:40,567 --> 00:14:41,687
That looks tasty.

243
00:14:41,687 --> 00:14:42,947
Mm-hmm.

244
00:14:46,507 --> 00:14:48,167
Kobayashi, can I have a watermelon?

245
00:14:48,527 --> 00:14:48,827
Huh?

246
00:14:48,847 --> 00:14:50,447
I didn't hear them mention watermelon.

247
00:14:51,247 --> 00:14:53,467
No, Lady Toru bought one yesterday.

248
00:14:53,587 --> 00:14:55,007
Wow, you're very observant.

249
00:14:55,207 --> 00:14:56,547
Okay, we'll have it this afternoon.

250
00:14:57,407 --> 00:14:58,347
It's hot.

251
00:14:58,847 --> 00:14:59,987
So hot.

252
00:15:00,667 --> 00:15:01,907
So hot.

253
00:15:01,907 --> 00:15:21,347
What are you doing?

254
00:15:23,347 --> 00:15:24,267
Kobayashi.

255
00:15:27,787 --> 00:15:28,387
There.

256
00:15:28,667 --> 00:15:29,487
Are you ready for lunch?

257
00:15:30,247 --> 00:15:30,787
Yeah.

258
00:15:30,787 --> 00:15:32,607
Okay, I'll get it started.

259
00:15:32,787 --> 00:15:36,287
Do you think you could go downstairs and check the mailbox for me, pretty please?

260
00:15:37,447 --> 00:15:39,627
Can we have some mini-tomatoes?

261
00:15:41,387 --> 00:15:42,067
Ta-da!

262
00:15:42,347 --> 00:15:43,287
Easy to make!

263
00:15:43,287 --> 00:15:55,727
Wow.

264
00:15:56,167 --> 00:15:56,867
Air mail, huh?

265
00:15:57,867 --> 00:16:01,287
I wonder if it's from that new friend you said you made in New York the other day.

266
00:16:02,727 --> 00:16:03,587
Oh, Chloe.

267
00:16:03,887 --> 00:16:06,267
She says she wants to come over and play with me.

268
00:16:06,487 --> 00:16:08,327
Is it okay if she stays for a bit?

269
00:16:08,467 --> 00:16:09,147
Sure, of course.

270
00:16:09,607 --> 00:16:10,007
Really?

271
00:16:10,847 --> 00:16:11,767
Oh, boy!

272
00:16:11,767 --> 00:16:12,947
I can't wait to meet her.

273
00:16:18,767 --> 00:16:20,007
So sweet!

274
00:16:23,047 --> 00:16:25,187
Kobayashi, we don't have any more tea.

275
00:16:25,607 --> 00:16:25,887
Huh?

276
00:16:26,047 --> 00:16:26,887
Out already?

277
00:16:27,587 --> 00:16:29,647
If I don't make any, we only have milk.

278
00:16:30,327 --> 00:16:30,807
Oh, well.

279
00:16:31,207 --> 00:16:32,127
Let's go buy some.

280
00:16:32,987 --> 00:16:34,067
We're going out?

281
00:16:34,507 --> 00:16:35,467
Looks like it.

282
00:16:35,467 --> 00:16:38,007
Hana, where's your hat?

283
00:16:38,707 --> 00:16:39,547
I got it.

284
00:16:41,767 --> 00:16:43,147
Let's go, please.

285
00:16:43,467 --> 00:16:44,287
I'm here.

286
00:16:44,847 --> 00:16:45,367
Hat?

287
00:16:45,367 --> 00:16:49,007
Where are we going?

288
00:16:49,567 --> 00:16:50,387
I don't know yet.

289
00:16:50,587 --> 00:16:51,227
Let's explore.

290
00:16:53,087 --> 00:16:53,527
Oh.

291
00:16:54,487 --> 00:16:57,467
Wonder, wonder, wonder, wandering.

292
00:16:59,067 --> 00:17:01,207
Maybe you'll find some things for your picture diary.

293
00:17:01,987 --> 00:17:04,547
I can look for stuff for my research, too.

294
00:17:05,087 --> 00:17:06,487
I hope you find something amazing.

295
00:17:07,487 --> 00:17:07,707
Hmm?

296
00:17:08,107 --> 00:17:12,807
Lady Toru said I should research foods from the other world that you might like her to cook sometime.

297
00:17:13,007 --> 00:17:14,167
Maybe as a surprise.

298
00:17:14,567 --> 00:17:15,167
I see.

299
00:17:16,567 --> 00:17:18,087
Why don't we do something else now?

300
00:17:23,667 --> 00:17:24,067
Ants.

301
00:17:24,447 --> 00:17:24,707
Hmm?

302
00:17:25,307 --> 00:17:26,267
Lots of ants.

303
00:17:26,267 --> 00:17:29,927
Oh, you're right.

304
00:17:30,487 --> 00:17:32,727
I wonder if they have a little home under that manhole.

305
00:17:33,347 --> 00:17:33,827
Manhole?

306
00:17:34,427 --> 00:17:35,487
But for ants?

307
00:17:36,027 --> 00:17:36,247
Hmm.

308
00:17:36,707 --> 00:17:37,987
It's actually made for a human.

309
00:17:39,467 --> 00:17:43,167
There's a path for sewage beneath the ground here that runs all over the city.

310
00:17:43,867 --> 00:17:45,967
Does that mean there are more lids on the ground?

311
00:17:46,507 --> 00:17:46,907
Mm-hmm.

312
00:17:47,207 --> 00:17:47,427
Yep.

313
00:17:47,687 --> 00:17:48,707
Way too many, in fact.

314
00:17:48,947 --> 00:17:49,387
Oh.

315
00:17:50,667 --> 00:17:51,147
Okay.

316
00:17:51,367 --> 00:17:52,147
I'll hunt them.

317
00:17:52,427 --> 00:17:52,707
Huh?

318
00:17:56,267 --> 00:17:57,627
I found another one.

319
00:17:59,347 --> 00:18:00,487
Hey, very good.

320
00:18:00,827 --> 00:18:02,087
This another research project?

321
00:18:02,667 --> 00:18:03,507
Over there.

322
00:18:07,167 --> 00:18:08,987
You'll find a lot of them on this street.

323
00:18:09,527 --> 00:18:10,847
This one's the same.

324
00:18:11,687 --> 00:18:12,887
This one's square.

325
00:18:13,067 --> 00:18:14,307
That's for a fire hydrant.

326
00:18:14,767 --> 00:18:17,027
This one's similar but kind of different.

327
00:18:17,887 --> 00:18:18,327
Right.

328
00:18:19,007 --> 00:18:19,447
Kinda...

329
00:18:20,587 --> 00:18:21,667
Kobayashi!

330
00:18:22,287 --> 00:18:24,167
I found another one.

331
00:18:24,807 --> 00:18:25,407
Great.

332
00:18:26,267 --> 00:18:30,907
Kobayashi, are you okay?

333
00:18:31,127 --> 00:18:31,707
Oh, sure.

334
00:18:32,187 --> 00:18:34,427
That was a great exercise for an indoor person.

335
00:18:36,147 --> 00:18:36,827
Oh.

336
00:18:40,007 --> 00:18:41,667
This is so cool.

337
00:18:43,347 --> 00:18:43,767
Ow.

338
00:18:43,767 --> 00:18:53,707
I guess dragons can get a brain freeze, too.

339
00:18:54,867 --> 00:18:56,407
Yours looks very yummy.

340
00:18:56,967 --> 00:18:57,787
Do you want to try some?

341
00:18:58,447 --> 00:18:58,847
Yeah.

342
00:19:07,487 --> 00:19:08,387
Kobayashi, look.

343
00:19:08,387 --> 00:19:08,847
Hmm?

344
00:19:08,987 --> 00:19:09,427
Oh.

345
00:19:10,627 --> 00:19:11,447
Oh, wow.

346
00:19:11,687 --> 00:19:12,807
You found a colorful one.

347
00:19:13,767 --> 00:19:14,847
Looks interesting.

348
00:19:15,087 --> 00:19:16,127
Has it always been like that?

349
00:19:16,407 --> 00:19:18,987
It's weird that I've lived here so long and never noticed it.

350
00:19:19,227 --> 00:19:20,327
Is it some kind of character?

351
00:19:21,847 --> 00:19:23,167
It's Mr. Quiet.

352
00:19:23,467 --> 00:19:24,647
So you recognize him.

353
00:19:25,327 --> 00:19:26,907
He's the talk of the town.

354
00:19:27,307 --> 00:19:28,147
That's enough.

355
00:19:28,147 --> 00:19:32,067
Oh, great.

356
00:19:32,407 --> 00:19:33,367
Random monsoon?

357
00:19:33,607 --> 00:19:34,287
Let's go, Kana.

358
00:19:35,227 --> 00:19:35,427
Retreating.

359
00:19:41,427 --> 00:19:43,687
Are you hanging in there, Kana?

360
00:19:44,147 --> 00:19:44,667
Yeah.

361
00:19:44,927 --> 00:19:46,227
I protected my notebook.

362
00:19:46,487 --> 00:19:47,227
Good for you.

363
00:19:47,227 --> 00:19:49,467
Well, we may as well just go swimming now.

364
00:19:53,047 --> 00:19:54,347
What was that?

365
00:19:54,487 --> 00:19:55,327
That's pretty cool.

366
00:19:58,447 --> 00:20:00,087
Well, what do you expect?

367
00:20:00,307 --> 00:20:02,047
Just a typical summer downpour.

368
00:20:02,807 --> 00:20:04,187
Typical downpour?

369
00:20:05,407 --> 00:20:07,507
Rainy, rainy, rain, rain.

370
00:20:08,107 --> 00:20:08,227
Downpour.

371
00:20:09,107 --> 00:20:10,227
It's a rainy monsoon.

372
00:20:11,087 --> 00:20:12,207
Stop summoning it.

373
00:20:12,827 --> 00:20:13,607
Howl away.

374
00:20:14,067 --> 00:20:15,427
Thunder so strong.

375
00:20:15,787 --> 00:20:16,347
Sing a song of rain.

376
00:20:16,347 --> 00:20:17,147
This is not good.

377
00:20:17,747 --> 00:20:18,867
Watch out for the equipment.

378
00:20:19,807 --> 00:20:20,987
It's Mr. Quiet.

379
00:20:21,507 --> 00:20:22,827
The head is too big.

380
00:20:22,827 --> 00:20:24,547
That's what the manhole picture was of?

381
00:20:24,547 --> 00:20:25,147
Put your head.

382
00:20:25,387 --> 00:20:25,747
Yes.

383
00:20:32,987 --> 00:20:34,327
Poor ladybug.

384
00:20:34,907 --> 00:20:35,487
Oh, yeah.

385
00:20:35,967 --> 00:20:37,327
It must have got washed away.

386
00:20:37,987 --> 00:20:38,867
Is she dead?

387
00:20:43,187 --> 00:20:44,047
It's alive.

388
00:20:44,047 --> 00:20:44,507
Oh, yay.

389
00:20:44,507 --> 00:20:51,827
It flew away.

390
00:20:51,827 --> 00:20:53,787
I'm sure that it's going back home.

391
00:20:53,827 --> 00:20:55,667
Oh, she has a home?

392
00:20:56,327 --> 00:20:57,367
Everyone does.

393
00:20:58,827 --> 00:20:59,307
Oh.

394
00:21:02,907 --> 00:21:03,467
Rainbow.

395
00:21:03,467 --> 00:21:07,567
It sure looks like one.

396
00:21:08,067 --> 00:21:08,547
Mm-hmm.

397
00:21:09,067 --> 00:21:11,187
And now the rain's completely stopped.

398
00:21:12,107 --> 00:21:14,287
Toru and the others should be getting home soon, too.

399
00:21:15,627 --> 00:21:16,527
You ready, Kana?

400
00:21:18,427 --> 00:21:19,147
Come on.

401
00:21:19,147 --> 00:21:21,927
It's time to go home.

402
00:21:21,927 --> 00:21:22,007
Home.

403
00:21:25,007 --> 00:21:25,607
Home.

404
00:21:29,747 --> 00:21:31,907
Next time I want to bring a camera.

405
00:21:32,207 --> 00:21:32,847
You should.

406
00:21:34,527 --> 00:21:35,767
We're home.

407
00:21:35,967 --> 00:21:37,027
Welcome back.

408
00:21:37,147 --> 00:21:38,187
You're so late.

409
00:21:38,487 --> 00:21:39,247
Let's eat.

410
00:21:39,427 --> 00:21:40,607
I'm hungry, too.

411
00:21:40,607 --> 00:21:42,367
Where were you two all day today?

412
00:21:42,807 --> 00:21:43,167
Hmm.

413
00:21:43,547 --> 00:21:44,227
Here and there.

414
00:21:44,287 --> 00:21:45,227
It was so fun.

415
00:21:45,347 --> 00:21:45,687
Right?

416
00:21:45,947 --> 00:21:47,287
Something fun without me?

417
00:21:47,427 --> 00:21:47,927
No fair!

418
00:21:47,927 --> 00:21:49,367
Can we please eat?

419
00:21:49,367 --> 00:21:49,467
Eat!

420
00:23:19,927 --> 00:23:23,487
That's wicked.

421
00:23:23,927 --> 00:23:24,787
Huh? What is?

422
00:23:24,927 --> 00:23:27,787
Sorry, I'm still getting used to not being in the Big Apple.

423
00:23:28,047 --> 00:23:29,787
Kana, you're too easily influenced.

424
00:23:29,947 --> 00:23:32,187
Don't wait up. I'm going to a party with a friend.

425
00:23:32,227 --> 00:23:33,847
You're going to Psychoist to play, right?

426
00:23:36,347 --> 00:23:38,687
This week on Who's Rotten?

427
00:23:39,487 --> 00:23:39,967
Virgo.

